# Sentence casing

Use **sentence case** for all user-facing UI text across every dashboard and page (Overview, AI Search Performance, Prompt Tracking, Site Health, etc.).

## Rules

- Labels, headings, table headers, column headers, buttons, chips, tabs, nav items, KPI titles, and metric labels use sentence case.
- Example: `Primary metric`, not `PRIMARY METRIC` or `Primary Metric`.
- Example: `Finish setup`, not `Finish Setup`.
- Example: `Trend score`, not `TREND SCORE` or `Trend Score`.
- Example: `Recommended`, not `RECOMMENDED`.

## Exceptions

Keep established acronyms and product names in their conventional form:

- AI, SEO, GBP, URL, CTA, GA4, GSC, XML, SoV, AIO
- Brand / product names (e.g. Google Business Profile, Search Console, Go High Level)

## Do not

- Do not use Tailwind `uppercase`, `tracking-wide`, `tracking-wider`, `tracking-widest`, or CSS `text-transform: uppercase` on any user-facing label — including tooltip/popover eyebrows, section dividers, metric chips, and modal headers.
- Prefer `font-medium text-gray-500` (or the shared table `th` pattern) for column headers — never all-caps styling.
- Do not title-case every word in UI chrome (`Open Dashboard` → `Open dashboard`).
- Do not leave decorative symbols in column headers unless they are part of the metric name (e.g. remove `Δ` from `Trend score`).
- Wrong: `AI ANSWERS` (via `uppercase` class). Right: `AI answers`.

## When adding or editing copy

1. Default to sentence case.
2. If Figma shows all-caps for a label, still implement sentence case.
3. Before finishing any UI task, search the touched files for `uppercase`, `tracking-wider`, `tracking-widest`, and ALL-CAPS string literals and remove them.
4. Scope is the whole product UI — dashboards, modals, drawers, setup flows, and tooltips — not just the file you edited.
